n nothing while our opponent has back rank issues. }) 21... Rd5 { [%clk 0:01:44] } 22. Qc3 { [%clk 0:02:49] } Rfd8 { [%clk 0:01:41] doubling the rooks. Some good habits. } 23. h3 { [%clk 0:02:35] } Ne4 { [%clk 0:01:39] and now to the outpost. } 24. Qf3 { [%clk 0:02:26] } Rd3 { [%clk 0:01:21] } (24... Nd2 25. Qg3+ Kh7 26. Rc1 Ne4 { the fork doesn't work because of Qg3+ }) 25. Qh5 { [%clk 0:02:12] } Qf6 { [%clk 0:01:14] } (25... Ng3 26. Qxh6 Qc5+ 27. Kh2 Nxf1+ 28. Kh1 Rg3 { this line was also possible. The queen looks scary on h6 but does not have any checks. }) 26. Rxb7 { [%clk 0:02:05] } Ng3 { [%clk 0:01:05] trapping the queen. } 27. Rxf7 { [%clk 0:00:41] } (27. Qxf7+ Qxf7 28. Rxf7 Kxf7 { This was needed to force the queen trade. }) 27... Qd4+ { [%clk 0:01:03] 0-1 Black wins on time. Opponent rage quits. } 28. Kh2 Nxf1+ 29. Kh1 Ng3+ 30. Kh2 Nxh5 { brutal. } 0-1

