{ https://youtu.be/LU87kQCjL1g?si=H4zbOpXzpkEta6kN&t=3790 } 1. e4 { [%clk 0:04:55] } e6 { [%clk 0:04:57] } 2. d4 { [%clk 0:04:49] } d5 { [%clk 0:04:55] } 3. Nd2 { [%clk 0:04:48] The Tarrasch variation. More common at higher ELOs. GM Daniel Naroditski (RIP) recommended this against the French https://youtu.be/JKxlT73xpYo?si=V2mfZRGB6f61nkF0 and it was also recommended by Aman in the original Habits series, although in the latest Habits he stuck to the exchange throughout. } c5 { [%clk 0:04:39] We play c5 against the Tarrasch as the main line. Aman has mentioned another line involving the waiting moves h6 a6 which we see later in the speed run. } 4. Ngf3 { [%clk 0:04:46] } cxd4 { [%clk 0:04:29] We take here. So far this has looked very similar to how we play the advanced. } 5. exd5 { [%clk 0:04:43] } Qxd5 { [%clk 0:04:26] Again recapturing with the queen, which can't be bothered by the knights. Aman says that this is essentially the main line. } 6. Bc4 { [%clk 0:04:41] } Qd7 { [%clk 0:04:19] With a6, b5 ideas followed by Bb7. } 7. O-O { [%clk 0:04:38] } Nc6 { [%clk 0:04:07] } 8. Nb3 { [%clk 0:04:35] } a6 { [%clk 0:03:55] giving the pawn back, which we've not bothered trying to hold on to. } 9. Nbxd4 { [%clk 0:04:29] } Nxd4 { [%clk 0:03:44] } 10. Nxd4 { [%clk 0:04:27] We have given back the pawn and white has two minor pieces developed and is castled vs us who have our queen developed off the back rank, a terrible LSB, and king in the middle of the board. However, the engine evaluation is equal. } Nf6 { [%clk 0:03:08] Aman considered b5 but feels it's slightly premature. } 11. Bg5 { [%clk 0:04:24] } Be7 { [%clk 0:02:54] focussing on development but b5 still planned. } 12. c3 { [%clk 0:04:20] } b5 { [%clk 0:02:47] And now the time is right. 3rd top engine move. } 13. Bb3 { [%clk 0:04:09] Re1 coming next? } Bb7 { [%clk 0:01:29] Re1 is a concern but Aman thinks that Ne4 as a resource is enough. } 14. Re1 { [%clk 0:04:05] } Bd5 { [%clk 0:01:03] Thinking through the lines Aman sees complications in Ne4 involving the queen coming to g4 and elects for this bishop move instead, defending the pawn. } 15. Bxd5 { [%clk 0:03:47] } Qxd5 { [%clk 0:00:55] "I guess Nxd5 is the safer move but this is the move I want to do". } 16. Qb3?? { [%clk 0:03:14] drops the hanging bishop } Qxg5 { [%clk 0:00:40] } 17. Nc6? { [%clk 0:03:11] Nxe6 was called for. Aman was planning for Ra7 in response to that. } (17. Nxe6 fxe6 18. Qxe6 Ra7 { Qc5, Nd7 were stronger options that Aman noticed in the post match analysis. } 19. Qc8+ Kf7 20. Qxh8 { We are still winning in this line }) 17... Qd5 { [%clk 0:00:32] } 18. Nxe7 { [%clk 0:03:05] } Qxb3 { [%clk 0:00:30] } 19. axb3 { [%clk 0:03:00] } Kxe7 { [%clk 0:00:30] 0-1 Black wins. } 0-1

