{ https://youtu.be/rH0atZvwYpw?si=kDacbeC8GLEdN3g9&t=5713 } 1. e4 { [%clk 0:05:00] } e6 { [%clk 0:05:00] } 2. d4 { [%clk 0:04:59] } d5 { [%clk 0:04:59] } 3. exd5 { [%clk 0:04:58] } exd5 { [%clk 0:04:57] } 4. h3 { [%clk 0:04:56] wasting time. This is usually a sign that the SW is possible. } Bd6 { [%clk 0:04:55] Going for our set up. Actually this is a flexible move as our conservative set up, aggressive set up, and even the SW, are all still possible from here. } 5. Bd3 { [%clk 0:04:55] } Nc6 { [%clk 0:04:50] Now committing to the aggressive set up. } (5... f5 6. Qh5+ g6 7. Qe2+ Kf7 { Early attempt to force a SW fall to this. }) (5... c6 6. Nf3 f5 7. O-O Nf6 8. Re1+ Ne4 9. c4 { Always our Achilles heel. } O-O { again, the wasted h3 move allows us to get in the SW. Opponent needs to strike with c4 right away to stop us. Even here though white is better. } 10. Nc3 Nd7 11. cxd5 cxd5 12. Nxd5 Ndf6 13. Nc3 { we just can't deal with this pressure on our d pawn if the opponent knows what they are doing. }) 6. c3 { [%clk 0:04:54] } Nge7 { [%clk 0:04:49] } 7. Nf3 { [%clk 0:04:53] } Bf5 { [%clk 0:04:48] Aman said he would have preferred Bg4 but it wasn't possible. Offering to trade our bad bishop. } 8. O-O { [%clk 0:04:51] } Qd7 { [%clk 0:04:46] Here Aman notes that Bxh3 is an idea here. } 9. Bg5 { [%clk 0:04:40] always like to see this. } f6 { [%clk 0:04:41] } 10. Bh4 { [%clk 0:04:38] } Bxd3 { [%clk 0:03:39] He elects to trade here, with one benefit being to open up f5 for the knight. } (10... Bxh3 11. gxh3 Qxh3 12. Bg3 Bxg3 13. fxg3 Qxg3+ 14. Kh1 { In the end Aman ruled this out as he is left with only the queen as attacker and it is too slow to bring in other pieces to support. }) 11. Qxd3 { [%clk 0:04:37] } Nf5 { [%clk 0:03:38] the main idea behind the previous trade. Our knight joins the attack. } 12. Re1+ { [%clk 0:04:32] } Nce7 { [%clk 0:03:29] Blocks the check and prepares the knight to be rerouted to the attack. } 13. g4 { [%clk 0:04:25] } Nxh4 { [%clk 0:03:23] } 14. Nxh4 { [%clk 0:04:23] } O-O-O { [%clk 0:03:17] Preparing h5. Our opponent seems oblivious to the threat. } 15. Nd2 { [%clk 0:04:21] } h5 { [%clk 0:03:09] threatening to blast the king side wide open with both rooks ready to join the party. } 16. Nf5 { [%clk 0:04:19] } hxg4 { [%clk 0:03:04] } 17. hxg4 { [%clk 0:04:17] kb8 an idea here. } Nxf5 { [%clk 0:02:15] Aman ends up choosing this line, which wins a pawn for certain, and leaves us better in the end game. } (17... Ng6 18. Nxd6+ Qxd6 19. Qxg6 Qh2+ 20. Kf1 Qh1+ 21. Ke2 Rde8+ 22. Ne4 Qxe4+ 23. Qxe4 Rxe4+ 24. Kf3 Rh3+ 25. Kg2 { Aman looked at this line but there is no mate to be found. }) (17... Bh2+ 18. Kg2 Ng6 19. Nd6+ Bxd6 20. Qxg6 Rh4 21. Kf3 Rdh8 { This may have been a better line. Aman looked at Bh2+ in the post game analysis. }) 18. Qxf5 { [%clk 0:04:15] } Qxf5 { [%clk 0:02:14] } 19. gxf5 { [%clk 0:04:14] } Rh5 { [%clk 0:02:14] } 20. Nf3 { [%clk 0:04:02] } Rxf5 { [%clk 0:02:08] winning the pawn. } 21. Kg2 { [%clk 0:04:00] } Rh8 { [%clk 0:02:02] with Rfh5 ideas to double the rooks. } 22. Rh1 { [%clk 0:03:59] } Rfh5 { [%clk 0:02:01] } 23. Rxh5 { [%clk 0:03:57] } Rxh5 { [%clk 0:02:01] } 24. Rg1 { [%clk 0:03:49] } Kd7 { [%clk 0:01:57] to take control of the e file. With g5 ideas. } 25. Kf1 { [%clk 0:03:47] } g5 { [%clk 0:01:56] } 26. Ke2 { [%clk 0:03:46] } Ke6 { [%clk 0:01:52] further activating the king. } 27. Ne1 { [%clk 0:03:43] Knight headed to d3? } Rh2 { [%clk 0:01:41] } 28. Nd3 { [%clk 0:03:40] } Kf5 { [%clk 0:01:33] } 29. Kf3 { [%clk 0:03:21] } g4+ { [%clk 0:01:26] } 30. Ke3 { [%clk 0:03:11] } (30. Rxg4 Rh3+ 31. Rg3 Bxg3 32. fxg3 { on takes we have this line. }) 30... Rh3+ { [%clk 0:01:17] } 31. Ke2 { [%clk 0:03:09] } Kg5 { [%clk 0:01:04] make way for an f pawn push and connecting these pawns. } 32. b3 { [%clk 0:02:50] } f5 { [%clk 0:00:57] } 33. c4 { [%clk 0:02:48] } c6 { [%clk 0:00:56] } 34. cxd5 { [%clk 0:02:21] } cxd5 { [%clk 0:00:55] } 35. b4 { [%clk 0:02:07] } f4 { [%clk 0:00:51] } 36. a4 { [%clk 0:02:03] } Kf5 { [%clk 0:00:46] } 37. Kd2 { [%clk 0:01:56] } b6 { [%clk 0:00:41] stopping the knight from going to c5. } 38. Kc3 { [%clk 0:01:53] } Bxb4+ { [%clk 0:00:36] removing the defender/deflection tactic. } 39. Kxb4 { [%clk 0:01:48] } Rxd3 { [%clk 0:00:35] 0-1 Black wins. And our opponent has had enough } 0-1

